   "subject": "upcoming workshops: March 21 Kansas City; April 1 and 3, MSU (+zoom); + STATA journal paper",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-size:16px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif\"><section style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><article style=\"box-sizing:border-box\"><div style=\"box-sizing:border-box;padding-top:5px;padding-bottom:5px\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">I will be giving a workshop on March\r\n21 in Kansas City prior to the meetings of the <span style=\"border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">The\r\nAssociation for Education Finance and Policy </span><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Details at the bottom of this message. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Register at: <a href=\"http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop#register\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop%23register&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244527685000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vaI5vBUz9T34pHVgkFj0F\">http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop#register</a><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> </span></p><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);border-top-width:initial;border-right-width:initial;border-left-width:initial;border-style:none none solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-bottom-color:rgb(204,204,204);padding:0in 0in 7pt\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;border-width:initial;border-style:none;padding:0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\">I will also be teaching my approaches to Sensitivity/Robustness as part of my course on multiple regression.</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\">  </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\">This will be April 1 and 3 from 1pm-2:20pm in\r\nroom 275 Giltner Hall at Michigan State, but you can also join via zoom: </span><a href=\"https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244527685000&amp;usg=AOvVaw111DHjgAaTi2FpO5WGhsDd\">https://msu.zoom.us/j/783760435</a><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">. \r\nDownload for 2 minutes and you will be ready.  You can call in at <a href=\"tel:(415)%20762-9988\" value=\"+14157629988\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(415) 762-9988</a>\r\nor <a href=\"tel:(646)%20568-7788\" value=\"+16465687788\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(646) 568-7788</a>. Meeting ID is 783-760-435</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;border-width:initial;border-style:none;padding:0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;border-width:initial;border-style:none;padding:0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\">Both are based on materials at: </span><a href=\"https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/research.htm#causal\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/research.htm%23causal&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244527685000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZJjjw7Sw0fNCaXXtsAf2n\">https://msu.edu/~kenfrank/research.htm#causal</a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;border-width:initial;border-style:none;padding:0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\"><br></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;border-width:initial;border-style:none;padding:0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\">There will also be a paper on Konfound coming out in\r\nthe STATA journal. Details at the bottom of this message.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal;border-width:initial;border-style:none;padding:0in\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\"> </span><br></p></div><div style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);padding:0in 0in 7pt;border-top-width:initial;border-style:none none solid;border-right-width:initial;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-bottom-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:initial\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;padding:0in;border-width:initial;border-style:none;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">What would it take to Change your Inference? Quantifying the Discourse about Causal Inferences in the Social Sciences<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;padding:0in;border-width:initial;border-style:none;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">March 21 Kansas City Missouri, AEFP. </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\"> </span><a href=\"http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop#register\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif;font-size:12pt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop%23register&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244527685000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vaI5vBUz9T34pHVgkFj0F\">http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop#register</a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0.0001pt;padding:0in;border-width:initial;border-style:none;line-height:normal\"><br></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;line-height:normal\"><i><span style=\"padding:0in;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Motivation</span></i><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br>Statistical inferences are often challenged because of uncontrolled bias. There may be bias due to uncontrolled confounding variables or non-random selection into a sample. We will answer the question about what it would take to change an inference by formalizing the sources of bias and quantifying the discourse about causal inferences in terms of those sources. For example, we will transform challenges such as “But the inference of a treatment effect might not be valid because of pre-existing differences between the treatment groups” to questions such as “How much bias must there have been due to uncontrolled pre-existing differences to make the inference invalid?” “QQQ% of the cases would have to be replaced with cases with no treatment effect to change the inference.”<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;line-height:normal\"><i><span style=\"padding:0in;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Approaches</span></i><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br>In part I we will use Rubin’s causal model to interpret how much bias there must be to invalidate an inference in terms of replacing observed cases with counterfactual cases or cases from an unsampled population. In part II, we will quantify the robustness of causal inferences in terms of correlations associated with unobserved variables or in unsampled populations. Calculations for bivariate and multivariate analysis will be presented using an app: <a href=\"http://konfound-it.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://konfound-it.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244527685000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0e60Ije0p03iyaDAaYTFi1\"><span style=\"padding:0in;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;color:rgb(51,122,183)\">http://konfound-it.com</span></a> as well as macros in STATA and R and a spreadsheet for calculating indices [KonFound-it!].<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;line-height:normal\"><i><span style=\"padding:0in;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Format</span></i><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><br>The format will be a mixture of presentation, individual exploration, and group work. Participants may include graduate students and professors, although all must be comfortable with basic regression and multiple regression. Participants should bring their own laptop, or be willing to work with another student who has a laptop. Participants may choose to bring to the course an example of an inference from a published study or their own work, as well as data analyses they are currently conducting.<a name=\"m_1618659310849332580_register\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">The workshop will be provided by <b><span style=\"padding:0in;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext\">Ken Frank</span></b> MSU Foundation Professor of Sociometrics in Measurement and Quantitative Methods at Michigan State University in Counseling, Educational Psychology and Special Education.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\">Register at: <a href=\"http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop#register\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop%23register&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244527685000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vaI5vBUz9T34pHVgkFj0F\">http://aefpweb.org/conferences/inference-workshop#register</a><u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"center\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);text-align:center\"><a name=\"m_1618659310849332580_OLE_LINK50\" rel=\"nofollow\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%\"><br></span></b></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"center\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);text-align:center\"><a name=\"m_1618659310849332580_OLE_LINK50\" rel=\"nofollow\"><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%\">KONFOUND: Stata Module to Quantify Robustness of Causal Inferences</span></b></a><b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:107%\"><u></u><u></u></span></b></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" align=\"center\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);text-align:center\">Ran Xu<sup>1*</sup>,\r\nKenneth A. Frank<sup>2</sup>, Spiro J. Maroulis<sup>3</sup>, Joshua M. Rosenberg<sup>4<u></u><u></u></sup></p><p style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><sup><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">1</span></sup><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering, Virginia Tech,\r\nFalls Church, Virginia, USA<u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><sup><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">2 </span></sup><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <span><a href=\"http://ed-web3.educ.msu.edu/CEPSE/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ed-web3.educ.msu.edu/CEPSE/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244527685000&amp;usg=AOvVaw357SicxehKZMCKtSgnJ_Je\">Department\r\nof Counseling, Educational Psychology and Special Education</a></span>,\r\nMichigan State University, East Lansing, Michigan, USA<u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><sup><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">3 </span></sup><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;background:#f7f6f6\"> </span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">School of\r\nPublic Affairs, Arizona State University, Tempe, Arizona, USA<u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><sup><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">4  </span></sup><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">College of Education, Health, and Human Sciences,\r\nUniversity of Tennessee, Knoxville, Tennessee, USA<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><sup>* </sup>Correspondence to <span><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ra...@vt.edu</a></span><u><u></u><u></u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51)\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51)\">Abstract. </b><font color=\"#333333\">Statistical\r\nmethods that quantify the discourse about causal inferences in terms of\r\npossible sources of biases, also known as “robustness or sensitivity analysis,”\r\nare becoming increasingly important to a variety of social-science fields, such\r\nas public policy, sociology, and education. A series of recent works by Frank and\r\ncolleagues on robustness analysis extends earlier methods. We implement these\r\nrecent developments in STATA. In particular, we provide <a name=\"m_1618659310849332580_OLE_LINK52\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a></font><a name=\"m_1618659310849332580_OLE_LINK51\" rel=\"nofollow\"><font color=\"#000000\">STATA routines to\r\nquantify the % bias necessary to invalidate an inference from a Rubin causal\r\nmodel framework, as well as the robustness of causal inferences in terms of\r\ncorrelations associated with unobserved variables.</font><font color=\"#333333\"><u></u><u></u></font></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> </span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);box-sizing:border-box\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);margin-bottom:0.0001pt;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"> <br></span></p></div></article></section></div></div>"
